<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabirdham district</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kawardha district</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kabirdham district is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with its headquarters at Kawardha. Formed in 1998 as Kawardha district and renamed in 2003, it covers the former princely state of Kawardha and the forested slopes of the Maikal range. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhoramdeo-temple">Bhoramdeo Temple</a> is its best-known monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kabirdham-district.jpg" alt="Kabirdham district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pankaj Oudhia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biodiversity_Rich_Maikal_Hills.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
